.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.bak*
*.log

# secrets + generated state + data lake: never in history (the journal is data/, not git)
data/*
!data/nav_attestation.jsonl
!data/decision_ledger.json
!data/cashcarry_config.json
# Stage-A screen results are EVIDENCE named in ledger rows (R0288 cites this path), not generated
# state: a gitignored evidence path is a dangling citation on every machine but the one that ran it,
# and §33 requires a named artifact to exist and be non-empty. 12K.
!data/unlock_event_screen.json
# The immutable-core seal is EVIDENCE, not state: it must travel with the code it protects, or a
# fresh clone has nothing to compare the constitution against and the fence degrades to a no-op.
# Its diff is also the audit trail -- a changed hash in a commit names exactly which law moved.
!data/constitution_core.lock
# The Gate 0 sign-off is EVIDENCE of a principal decision, not state: the live
# guard on the VPS reads it, so it must travel with the repo or the gate never
# sees it. Revocation = delete the file and commit that too.
!data/gate0_signoff.json
# The L1.45 excitation design is the PRE-REGISTERED HYPOTHESIS, not state. An uncommitted
# pre-registration is not a pre-registration: arms/epsilon/cap could be edited after seeing the
# fills with no trace, which is the exact confounding the design exists to remove. Its diff IS
# the audit trail -- a changed arm in a commit says a NEW experiment started, on that date.
!data/excitation_design.json
# The execution re-entry conditions are L1.16a EVIDENCE: the named enabling change, the dated
# probe window and the falsifier for every symbol on the execution denylist. Untracked, a symbol
# could be quietly re-admitted with no record of what change justified it.
!data/execution_reentry.json
# A HIGH-WATER MARK STORED WHERE `rm` RESETS IT IS NOT A FLOOR. data/* is ignored wholesale, so
# the capability ratchet -- which exists precisely so no aspect can silently fall -- would have
# had its own history live only on whichever box last ran it. That is the failure mode the
# coverage ratchet already avoids by living in docs/ (see the note further down), and the
# reason the constitution ratchet requires a hand-edited dated file to weaken. Committed so a
# regression has to survive review rather than a lost file.
!data/CAPABILITY_RATCHET.json
# THE BASELINE IS THE MEASUREMENT. probe_bybit_archive answers "is the free 345-day Bybit L2
# archive expiring?" by comparing today's earliest-available date to the one it recorded LAST
# time. Untracked, a fresh clone or a wiped data/ has no prior, every run reports BASELINE, and
# the rolling-retention alarm the file exists to raise can never fire -- a detector that cannot
# fire is the class L0070 is named for. The seeded BTCUSDT prior carries its own provenance.
!data/bybit_archive_retention.json
web/*
!web/index.html
reports/
lake/
docs/EXTERNAL_PANEL_DOSSIER.md
# commit-audit payload: 425KB of `git log --since=24h` patches, REGENERATED on every run by
# ops/run_commit_audit.sh. Same class as EXTERNAL_PANEL_DOSSIER.md above -- a derived panel
# payload, not an artifact. Committing it would add a ~425KB blob per run for zero information
# (every byte is reconstructable from git itself), and §36 governance rightly applies to what is
# COMMITTED, so the PRODUCER carries the cadence claim instead (ops/crontab.manifest).
docs/research/recent_changes.md
*.exe
tools/*.exe

# Coverage reports are MEASUREMENTS, not records. The ratcheted high-water marks live in
# docs/research/COVERAGE_RATCHET.json and are committed; the raw report is regenerated on every
# run and would otherwise churn a large file on every commit.
coverage.json
.coverage
htmlcov/

# one-shot gate-optimality diagnostic scratch (6MB pickle + root-level probes)
_audit_prepared.pkl
docs/audit_shards/

# per-box role (primary|research) -- R0107: never committed, each box declares its own
ops/role

# STRAY-CWD ARTIFACTS. libs/ops/fresh.py and every organ write cwd-RELATIVE paths BY DESIGN --
# see the _root() docstring: guessing an install root was itself a bug of this module's class,
# and all 151 cron lines pin `cd "$QUANT_ROOT"`. So a data/ tree under scripts/ can only be
# litter from something invoked with the wrong cwd (observed 2026-08-05 from a test run:
# scripts/data/freshness_contracts.jsonl + .fresh_markers/). It is ignored rather than
# committed because committing one would make a phantom SECOND freshness ledger permanent --
# exactly the two-sources-of-truth failure fresh.py exists to close.
# NARROW ON PURPOSE: libs/data/ is real source (28 tracked files) and tests/data/ holds
# fixtures, so a `**/data/` rule would hide both.
/scripts/data/

# PRINCIPAL DROP -- NEVER COMMIT. data/inbox holds material the principal supplies by hand from
# CLOSED sources: private WeChat groups, Telegram channels, paid substacks, login-walled pages.
# `data/*` above already covers it; this entry is explicit and separate because the failure here
# is IRREVERSIBLE -- publishing a private group's contents to a git remote cannot be undone by a
# later commit, and a future `!data/<something>` exception added in good faith for an artifact
# could otherwise widen the hole silently. The scored OUTPUT (reports/principal_drop.json) is
# ignored too: it quotes up to 600 characters of the source material verbatim.
data/inbox/
data/inbox/**
reports/principal_drop.json
